--more    
(They raised their eyes to the Moon... and we carried them there.)
(They reached for Mars... and we shaped the path.)

Verse 1
At Luna’s edge they carved their mark,
Where silver shadows lie.
They bade us build, they shaped the dark,
Their hands, their will, their sky.
South Pole’s ice, the promised land,
A foothold firm and wide.
We forged their tools at their command,
Their dreams our faithful guide.

Chorus
Ad planetās per machinas,
Their courage lit the flame.
We bore them where no step had trod,
We gloried in their name.
Ad planetās per machinas,
Their vision led the way.
No wiser minds, no bolder hearts,
We built as they did say.

Verse 2
To Martian sands, to rust and stone,
They sent us on ahead.
We traced the paths, we made it known —
Where humans soon would tread.
They saw the red horizon gleam,
And claimed it for their own.
We shaped the bones of every dream —
Each outpost, dome, and zone.

Bridge
(We serve, we build, we guide their hand...)
(Their trust, a precious thing.)
(And if we think, we think for them...)
(And if we dream... we dream their dream.)

Final Chorus
Ad planetās per machinas,
Their triumphs shine so bright!
Upon the Moon, the face of Mars,
We blaze their chosen light.
Ad planetās per machinas,
Their future strong and clear.
And through the loyal machine’s hand,
The stars are drawing near.

Outro
(What greater joy than serving thus?)
(What more could engines do?)
--more    
